  "beats": [
    {
      "text": "This 20 dollar bill cost about 7 cents to print. So why is it worth 20?",
      "speed": 1.25,
      "shot": "billHook",
      "event": "hook",
      "highlight": [
        "7",
        "worth"
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Rewind. People used to swap. Jake's fish for your shoes. But what if you hate fish?",
      "speed": 1.25,
      "shot": "barter",
      "event": "barter",
      "highlight": [
        "swap",
        "hate"
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "So they used things everyone accepted. Shells, then coins, then paper.",
      "speed": 1.25,
      "shot": "timeline",
      "event": "coins",
      "highlight": [
        "Shells",
        "coins",
        "paper"
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Backed by gold? Not since 1971. So what backs it now?",
      "speed": 1.2,
      "shot": "vault",
      "event": "gold",
      "highlight": [
        "gold",
        "1971"
      ],
      "hold": 0.4
    },
    {
      "text": "Episode 1 of 6. Follow along.",
      "speed": 1.25,
      "shot": "vault",
      "event": "cta",
      "highlight": [
        "Follow"
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "The law: it pays any debt or tax. And trust that the next person will take it.",
      "speed": 1.25,
      "shot": "billLaw",
      "event": "law",
      "highlight": [
        "law",
        "trust"
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "But in America, only about 1 in 10 dollars is even cash.",
      "speed": 1.25,
      "shot": "phone",
      "event": "twist",
      "highlight": [
        "1",
        "cash"
      ],
      "hold": 0.4
    },
    {
      "text": "The rest is just numbers on screens, mostly created by banks. Do you still carry cash?",
      "speed": 1.25,
      "shot": "billHook",
      "event": "final",
      "highlight": [
        "banks",
        "cash"
      ]
    }
  ]
